  faqEntries:
  - type: 1
    text: Do you know why is vinegar added so early?
    answer: 'Vinegar does more than season. It stops the blood from clotting too
      quickly and tames its mineral intensity. Pre-colonial Filipinos discovered
      this long before chemistry explained why it works. '
  - type: 1
    text: Do you know what is the classic pairing for dinuguan?
    answer: "Filipino tradition pairs dinuguan with \u201Cputo\u201D, soft steamed
      rice cakes. The puto\u2019s gentle sweetness balances the stew\u2019s deep,
      savory richness in a way few other combinations can."
  - type: 1
    text: Do you know if dinuguan the same across the Philippines?
    answer: "The dish wears many names. Ilokanos call it \u201Cdinardaraan\u201D.
      Kapampangans say \u201Ctid-tad babi\u201D. Cebuanos call it \u201Cdugo-dugo\u201D.
      In Bulacan, \u201Ctinumis\u201D even adds \u201Cmiswa\u201D noodles. Same spirit,
      different accents."
